KG42.register("source_edge_archive-c8dd64cb86fd129e6381a8f2",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.demand","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","target":"KG31-e3df7b859b17cba0","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R001::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::bidding.demand","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Appendix B's illustrated SDR interaction: Prosumer A's heater-demand schedule submitted to the coordinator. | Demand-bidding iteration under the paper's proposed last-defence mechanism. | Illustrated combined bid-count and ramping-rate step length control. | Iterative energy bidding using the bid-count form of step length control. | Proposed practical enforcement of ramping-rate step length control in P2P energy bidding. | Requested-energy bid updates in the iterative simulation's ramping-rate step length control. | Requested-energy quantities within SDR energy bids. | SDR bidding in the paper's two GB residential case-study sets, with accurate generation and demand forecasts assumed.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV07","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-14","v141-b-g07-ev-15"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"e3cfbd5effcb9c68e54d2f4416f0080e4618fa9301aeca224af42290b38cfde1","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","target_definition":"The coordinator must reject requested-energy bids exceeding the prescribed ramping rate, thereby limiting demand-bid updates. Scope: Proposed practical enforcement of ramping-rate step length control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a bid exceeds the prescribed ramping rate. The coordinator limits demand-bid updates by uniformly randomly selecting participants whose energy bids must remain unchanged for that iteration. Scope: Iterative energy bidding using the bid-count form of step length control. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the restriction applies to participants selected for the forbidden-update set at the current iteration. Internal prices motivate updates to Prosumer A's submitted demand schedule to use excess local PV generation from Prosumer B. Scope: Appendix B's illustrated SDR interaction: Prosumer A's heater-demand schedule submitted to the coordinator. Condition: The unequal hourly internal buying prices in the illustrated iterations. Participants must submit their requested-energy quantities as part of the energy bids required at every iteration. Scope: Requested-energy quantities within SDR energy bids. The current requested-energy bid must lie within the previous bid plus or minus the ramping rate times the previous bid's absolute value. The resulting interval is clipped to the bid's lower and upper limits. Scope: Requested-energy bid updates in the iterative simulation's ramping-rate step length control. Condition: The ramping-rate form of step length control is adopted. Only rmp′ × 100% of energy bids may change, and each permitted demand-bid change is also restricted to ± rmp′ × 100%. Scope: Illustrated combined bid-count and ramping-rate step length control. Condition: The combined control with the broader ramping rate rmp′ is adopted. Demand bidding is assumed to be conducted on a day-ahead basis. Scope: SDR bidding in the paper's two GB residential case-study sets, with accurate generation and demand forecasts assumed. Demand-bidding iteration must terminate at the iteration limit, including when bids have not converged. Scope: Demand-bidding iteration under the paper's proposed last-defence mechanism. Condition: The predefined maximum iteration count is reached, whether or not convergence has been achieved.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator must reject requested-energy bids exceeding the prescribed ramping rate, thereby limiting demand-bid updates. Scope: Proposed practical enforcement of ramping-rate step length control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a bid exceeds the prescribed ramping rate.","expression":"\\text{accept}_{\\text{coord}}(e_i^{bid}) \\iff \\max(e_{i-1}^{bid}-\\Delta,\\,e^{min}) \\le e_i^{bid} \\le \\min(e_{i-1}^{bid}+\\Delta,\\,e^{max}),\\quad \\Delta=rmp\\,|e_{i-1}^{bid}|","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-e-bid-ramping"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-rmp","v141-c-R001-theta-prev-bid-ramping","v141-c-R001-theta-e-min","v141-c-R001-theta-e-max"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator limits demand-bid updates by uniformly randomly selecting participants whose energy bids must remain unchanged for that iteration. Scope: Iterative energy bidding using the bid-count form of step length control. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the restriction applies to participants selected for the forbidden-update set at the current iteration.","expression":"e_{i,j}^{bid}=e_{i-1,j}^{bid},\\quad \\forall j\\in \\mathcal{PA}^{forbid}\\subset \\mathcal{PA},\\quad |\\mathcal{PA}^{forbid}|\\ \\text{pre-defined}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-x-e-bid-forbid"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-theta-prev-bid-forbid"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g02-e23"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p07-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"This technique limits the number or ramping rate of the changing 2P energy/price bids to increase th","equation_id":"8","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Taking the energy bidding process in iterative implementation as an example, the step length control can be achieved by requiring each prosumer agent to limit the ramping rate of the bid at each iteration:\n                bid     min        bid             bid       max                     bid      max( e i − 1−Δ,e    ) \\leqslant e i  \\leqslant min( e i − 1 + Δ,e    ) Δ = rmp ·|e i − 1 |       (8) \nwhere i is the index of the current iteration during which the bid decision needs to be made, and rmp represents the ramping rate that takes a non-negative value. Formula (8) can be basically interpreted as follows: the value of the current energy bid, e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_i, should be bounded in a range, [e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}−Δ,e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}+Δ], which is speciﬁed by the ramping rate and the bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1}|. Besides, if the upper bound speciﬁed in this way exceeds the maximum limit of the energy bid e^{\\max}, it should be reduced to e^{\\max} by having min(e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1} + Δ,e^{\\max}). Similar operation applies to the case of the lower bound. Formula (8) should act as an additional constraint in the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of each prosumer agent."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is, e_{i,j}^{bid} = e_{i-1,j}^{bid}, j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} ⊂ 𝓟𝓐 (9) where j is the index of prosumer agent. 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. |𝓟𝓐^{forbid}|, is pre-defined. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"8","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e_{i-1}^{bid}|. Besides, if the upper bound specified in this way exceeds the maximum limit of the energy bid e^{max}, it should be reduced to e^{max} by having min(e_{i-1}^{bid} + Δ, e^{max}). Similar operation applies to the case of the lower bound. Formula (8) should act as an additional constraint in the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of each prosumer agent."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th itera- p tion. The number of the e","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"At each iteration, the elements of 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers. The number of prosumers forbidden affects the magnitude of energy and price change in the region at each iteration, thus potentially affecting the convergence performance."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3","anchor_text":"y g ( vergence obtained in this way may be far from the feasible optimum). ti th 3.3.3. Practical im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The first technique, step length control, limits the ramping rate of the bids in the bidding process. In practice, this can be realised by the coordinator through setting bidding rules in the implementation model, as described in Section 3.2.4, in a P2P energy sharing mechanism. For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit. Therefore, the step length control technique in simulation is able to suggest better bidding rules in the implementation model in practice."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is,\n   e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i,j} = e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1,j}    j \\in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} \\subset \\mathcal{PA}                                         (9)\nwhere j is the index of prosumer agent. \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. |\\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}|, is pre-deﬁned. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function. ... At each iteration, the elements of \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Appendix B's illustrated SDR interaction: Prosumer A's heater-demand schedule submitted to the coordinator. | Demand-bidding iteration under the paper's proposed last-defence mechanism. | Illustrated combined bid-count and ramping-rate step length control. | Iterative energy bidding using the bid-count form of step length control. | Proposed practical enforcement of ramping-rate step length control in P2P energy bidding. | Requested-energy bid updates in the iterative simulation's ramping-rate step length control. | Requested-energy quantities within SDR energy bids. | SDR bidding in the paper's two GB residential case-study sets, with accurate generation and demand forecasts assumed.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-EV07","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-14","v141-b-g07-ev-15"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.demand","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
